BT 1 0 0 1 4 307.8 Tm 1.3988 Tw 9 TL /F5 7.2 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Abstract) Tj (\227Predicting commercial flight arrival delays prior to gate departure) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.0016 Tw (poses formidable statistical challenges: models must strictly avoid post-departure) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.226857 Tw (target leakage while capturing complex interdependencies among airport) Tj T* 0 Tw .4745 Tw (congestion, scheduled block buffers, carrier network dynamics, and propagated) Tj T* 0 Tw .95632 Tw (inbound aircraft turnaround delays. In this paper, we establish an end-to-end) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.283886 Tw (framework comparing gradient boosted decision trees \(XGBoost, LightGBM\),) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.282629 Tw (linear baselines, and deep neural architectures \(Tabular Entity-Embedding) Tj T* 0 Tw .155378 Tw (MLP and Recurrent Temporal Networks\) evaluated on commercial US domestic) Tj T* 0 Tw .31624 Tw (flights from the Bureau of Transportation Statistics \(BTS 2015 dataset, 147,389) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.016533 Tw (flights across 358 calendar dates\). Operating strictly at decision epoch T - 60) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.9226 Tw (minutes prior to scheduled departure, our feature engineering encapsulates) Tj T* 0 Tw .5104 Tw (expanding empirical Bayes smoothed historical priors, hourly departure/arrival) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.652914 Tw (density, and leakage-safe inbound turnaround slack. Empirical evaluation) Tj T* 0 Tw .4466 Tw (under calendar-date chronological partitioning confirms that the Deep Tabular) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.7982 Tw (MLP with dense entity embeddings achieves the highest discriminative) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.1485 Tw (performance \(ROC AUC 0.6196, PR AUC 0.2319\), outperforming gradient) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.242578 Tw (boosted ensembles \(XGBoost ROC AUC 0.5982, PR AUC 0.2141; LightGBM) Tj T* 0 Tw .114733 Tw (ROC AUC 0.5582, PR AUC 0.1875\) and linear baselines \(ROC AUC 0.6159, PR) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.620978 Tw (AUC 0.2284\). Post-hoc Platt sigmoid calibration compresses the Brier score) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.3984 Tw (from 0.18734 to 0.13271 and reduces the Expected Calibration Error \(ECE\)) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.315927 Tw (from 0.2255 to 0.0389. Operating at decision threshold tau = 0.3637, the) Tj T* 0 Tw .448178 Tw (calibrated MLP satisfies the operational precision constraint \() Tj /F6 7.2 Tf 9 TL (\263) Tj /F5 7.2 Tf 9 TL ( 70%, achieving) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.96072 Tw (71.43% precision and 0.29% recall, capturing 0.3% of delayed flights\); we) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.04088 Tw (clarify that this represents a threshold-specific trade-off to minimize false alarms) Tj T* 0 Tw .7576 Tw (rather than overall model superiority. Finally, we formulate an offline tactical) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.1368 Tw (rescheduling simulation based on explicit operational assumptions. Evaluated) Tj T* 0 Tw .019143 Tw (on 21,866 test flights at risk threshold tau = 0.171, the policy intervenes on 2,905) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.244178 Tw (flights \(13.29% intervention rate\), capturing 759 actual delays \(21.69% delay) Tj T* 0 Tw .7211 Tw (coverage\) with 2,146 false alarm interventions. Under simulation assumptions,) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.617527 Tw (this yields an estimated 303 averted delays and 9,176.7 gross delay minutes) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.244178 Tw (saved. However, factoring in schedule friction \(7.5 penalty minutes per) Tj T* 0 Tw .41704 Tw (intervention, totaling 21,787.5 penalty minutes\) results in a negative net benefit) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.767886 Tw (of -12,610.8 minutes, demonstrating that proactive interventions impose) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.752178 Tw (substantial operational friction that exceeds gross savings under linear cost) Tj T* 0 Tw (models.) Tj T* ET
